{
    "background_story": "Everett was a British explorer who traveled to Ethiopia in the late 19th century. During his journeys, he became fascinated with the ancient traditions of the Ethiopian Empire. He was particularly drawn to the title of 'Negus', which referred to the Ethiopian monarch. Everett spent years studying the language, customs, and history of the region, earning him the respect of the local people. He eventually became an advisor to the Negus himself, using his knowledge to help modernize the country's infrastructure and education system. Everett's dedication to the Ethiopian people and their rich heritage earned him a place in the country's history as a trusted friend and ally. He remained in Ethiopia until his passing, leaving behind a legacy of cultural exchange and understanding.",
